 "news": {
  "date": "2026-10-06",
  "asof": "2026-10-07 11:31 UTC",
  "headline": "The S&P made its first record since August \u2014 on a move smaller than an ordinary day",
  "standfirst": "The S&P rose 0.58% to 7,818.93, its first record close since 13 August, and the Nasdaq posted its second consecutive record \u2014 and nothing on the macro board moved even one sigma. What made this record different from Monday\u2019s is measurable: ten of eleven sectors higher for a third session, the equal-weight index matching the cap-weighted gain at +0.6%, and 65.1% positive volume on the NYSE, the best since 2 September. Yields eased across the whole curve for the first time in a week \u2014 two-year \u22124.2bp to 4.791%, ten-year \u22123.6 to 5.275%, thirty-year \u22121.7 to 5.647% \u2014 one session against the four that went the other way. Constellation Energy rose 12.3% on a twenty-year, 3.6-gigawatt power agreement with Google; Alphabet rose 0.22%. In the book GOOG reached another closing high at 344.59 and all three holdings finished green, while OKTA ran to a new 52-week high of 226.44 and closed 218.67, giving back 3.4% from the peak at +1.79R. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged for a nineteenth session.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "CPI on the 13th \u00b7 then 28 October",
    "title": "One print, then three weeks of nothing",
    "items": [
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "CPI",
      "html": "<b>September CPI</b> \u2014 the only first-tier print before the Fed, and the referee on two rising ISM prices indices",
      "when": "Tue \u00b7 2026-10-13",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-fomc",
      "tag": "FOMC",
      "html": "<b>Fed decision</b> \u2014 October hike odds are 16%; the long end made a 52-week high the day before easing",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "GOOG",
      "html": "<b>Alphabet Q3 earnings</b> \u2014 the first read on $195-205bn of capex, now with 3.6GW of power contracted against it",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "AAPL",
      "html": "<b>Apple Q4 earnings</b> \u2014 the first iPhone 18 quarter and the first read on Ternus",
      "when": "Thu \u00b7 2026-10-29",
      "kind": "calendar"
     }
    ],
    "note": "<b>CPI on the 13th is the only thing between here and the Fed.</b> It arrives with two ISM prices indices accelerating \u2014 manufacturing at <b>77.9</b>, up 6.8 points, and services at <b>74.0</b>, a second month above 72 \u2014 against a core PCE that came in at 3.0% against 3.3% expected. A hot print turns the long end's behaviour from a supply story into an inflation story, which is the easier version to trade. A soft one leaves the thirty-year near 5.65% with no data to explain it, which is the harder one."
   }
  ],
  "ondeck": "<b>CPI on the 13th is the only thing between here and the Fed.</b> It arrives with two ISM prices indices accelerating \u2014 manufacturing at <b>77.9</b>, up 6.8 points, and services at <b>74.0</b>, a second month above 72 \u2014 against a core PCE that came in at 3.0% against 3.3% expected. A hot print turns the long end's behaviour from a supply story into an inflation story, which is the easier version to trade. A soft one leaves the thirty-year near 5.65% with no data to explain it, which is the harder one.",
